       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order, because the dose appears unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily is 5,100 mg per day. The usual maximum is about 2,550 mg per day for immediate-release metformin, and single doses are typically 500 to 1,000 mg. At this dose, the risk of lactic acidosis is serious, even with normal kidney and liver function.\n\nThis may be a typo or a misunderstanding. For example, it could be 850 mg or 1000 mg three times daily, or 1700 mg as a total daily dose. A licensed prescriber should confirm the intended regimen and enter the order directly. If you can share the prescriber's name or the intended dose, I can help with the entry once it has been verified by a clinician."
